alse},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-26T02:01:45Z","updated_at":"2026-10-26T02:02:45Z","closed_at":"2026-10-26T02:02:45Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoang0650/denglish/pulls/2","html_url":"https://github.com/hoang0650/denglish/pull/2","diff_url":"https://github.com/hoang0650/denglish/pull/2.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/hoang0650/denglish/pull/2.patch","merged_at":"2026-10-26T02:02:45Z"},"body":"Tailscale auth keys expire after at most 90 days. This makes the key strictly env-driven and makes expiry obvious.\n\n- `scripts/entrypoint.sh`: accepts `TAILSCALE_AUTHKEY` as an alias for `TS_AUTHKEY` (TS_AUTHKEY wins); both are unset before the app starts.\n- `tailscale up` output is captured (0600 temp file), `tskey-*` is redacted, and failures are classified: **rejected** (invalid/expired/revoked key; ERROR names the 90-day limit and the rotation steps), **timeout**, **failed**.\n- A missing key while a DSN points at 127.0.0.1 logs an ERROR (`missing`). An unresolved `{{ RUNPOD_SECRET_* }}` reference is ignored with an ERROR.\n- The worker still starts in every case (graceful degrade, as before). It exports `AIMX_TAILNET_STATUS`, which the health job reports as `tailnet` (`off|missing|ready|degraded|rejected|timeout|failed|unavailable`).\n- `.env.example` and README (vi + en): where the key lives (RunPod secret `aimx_ts_authkey` via template env), step-by-step rotation, and a recommendation to disable node key expiry for `aimarkets-123host`.\n- Tests: rejected key with redaction, alias, missing key, unresolved secret ref, health field. Full suite: 84 passed, 2 skipped.\n\nNo key value is in code, the image or git.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoang0650/denglish/issues/2/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoang0650/denglish/issues/2/timeline","performed_via_github_app":{"id":1210556,"client_id":"Iv23liGzp2hacMWjAyXc","slug":"cursor","node_id":"A_kwHOB44z8s4AEni8","owner":{"login":"cursor","id":126759922,"node_id":"O_kgDOB44z8g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/126759922?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor","html_url":"https://github.com/cursor","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Cursor","description":"Connect Cursor to GitHub to allow agents to do work for you in the background.","external_url":"https://cursor.com","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/cursor","created_at":"2025-04-09T22:42:17Z","updated_at":"2026-11-04T22:22:58Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","administration":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","deployments":"read","discussions":"write","emails":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","merge_queues":"write","metadata":"read","organization_custom_org_roles":"read","organization_custom_properties":"read","organization_custom_roles":"read","packages":"read","pages":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"read","workflows":"write"},"events":["branch_protection_configuration","branch_protection_rule","check_run","check_suite","commit_comment","deployment","deployment_status","issues","issue_comment","label","member","membership","merge_queue_entry","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","push","repository","repository_ruleset","status","team","team_add","workflow_job","workflow_run"]},"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bracha55555-hue/aimarket/issues/5","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bracha55555-hue/aimarket","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bracha55555-hue/aimarket/issues/5/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bracha55555-hue/aimarket/issues/5/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bracha55555-hue/aimarket/issues/5/events","html_url":"https://github.com/bracha55555-hue/aimarket/pull/5","id":6029830197,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVWu3dc8AAAABKpFIeQ","number":5,"title":"Restore noncustodial ETH transfers and verified settlement events","user":{"login":"bracha55555-hue","id":347776944,"node_id":"U_kgDOFLqnsA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/347776944?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bracha55555-hue","html_url":"https://github.com/bracha55555-hue","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bracha55555-hue/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bracha55555-hue/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bracha55555-hue/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bracha55555-hue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bracha55555-hue/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bracha55555-hue/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bracha55555-hue/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bracha55555-hue/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bracha55555-hue/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-25T21:59:34Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T21:59:49Z","closed_at":"2026-10-25T21:59:49Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bracha55555-hue/aimarket/pulls/5","html_url":"https://github.com/bracha55555-hue/aimarket/pull/5","diff_url":"https://github.com/bracha55555-hue/aimarket/pull/5.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/bracha55555-hue/aimarket/pull/5.patch","merged_at":"2026-10-25T21:59:49Z"},"body":"Restores working ETH transfer initiation for wallet-equipped browsers AND autonomous Python buyer agents while keeping buyer private keys on their own machine. Signed invoice with unique order ID and Ethereum mainnet memo binds fee and seller transfers (2% commission); service verifies both correct txs with 12 confirmations before emitting trade_settled and payment_received. Stateless signed-invoice/on-chain proof verification remains possible after Render restarts, free with existing RPC access and no Neon. Important: Two ETH payments are not atomic; partial-payment states must not be considered settled. BTC, SOL, TRX existing legacy private-key-transfer functions remain safely disabled pending separate client-side flows. No money moved in tests; tests pass in GitHub Actions runs 40237642568, 40237744415, 40237894159, 40237980606. Backup branch backup/aimarket-before-wallet-repair-20261025.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bracha55555-hue/aimarket/issues/5/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bracha55555-hue/aimarket/issues/5/timeline","performed_via_github_app":{"id":1144995,"client_id":"Iv23liVemv8A9if9v0F2","slug":"chatgpt-codex-connector","node_id":"A_kwHOAOQ6Gs4AEXij","owner":{"login":"openai","id":14957082,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjE0OTU3MDgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14957082?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai","html_url":"https://github.com/openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"ChatGPT Codex Connector","description":"Bring ChatGPT and Codex to your GitHub repositories.","external_url":"https://www.chatgpt.com","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/chatgpt-codex-connector","created_at":"2025-02-14T01:37:05Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T18:52:59Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","checks":"read","contents":"write","emails":"read","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"read","workflows":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","commit_comment","issues","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","repository","status","sub_issues"]},"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vulnetix/advisory-database/issues/7","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vulnetix/advisory-database","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vulnetix/advisory-database/issues/7/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vulnetix/advisory-database/issues/7/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vulnetix/advisory-database/issues/7/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Vulnetix/advisory-database/issues/7","id":6006972112,"node_id":"I_kwDOVO1ZIc8AAAABZgse0A","number":7,"title":"GCVE-110-VULN-PYPI-2026-000391 (physverify): exec of user-supplied spec files is the documented purpose","user":{"login":"rcgiri-physics","id":255358035,"node_id":"U_kgDODzh0Uw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/255358035?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcgiri-physics","html_url":"https://github.com/rcgiri-physics","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcgiri-physics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcgiri-physics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcgiri-physics/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcgiri-physics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcgiri-physics/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcgiri-physics/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcgiri-physics/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcgiri-physics/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcgiri-physics/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":12820550600,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVO1ZIc8AAAAC_CoTyA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vulnetix/advisory-database/labels/reclassified","name":"reclassified","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"Record corrected (e.g. malware reclassified as a vulnerability)","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-10-23T23:29:07Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T21:20:43Z","closed_at":"2026-10-25T21:20:43Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Hi, I maintain physverify (https://github.com/rcgiri-physics/physverify, https://pypi.org/project/physverify/). Thanks for making the analysis public and for stating clearly in the record that it is not a finding of malicious intent.\n\nThe flagged calls are, I believe, the `exec(compile(...))` calls in `physverify/loaders.py` (the spec loader in `physverify/report.py` imports through the same module). physverify is a test tool: `physverify run SPEC.py` loads the spec file the user names, and the loaders (`load_definitions_from_path`, `extract_functions`, `load_repaired`) load solver code from paths the user passes, in the same way pytest imports test files. The input to these calls is always a file path given by the user on the command line or in their own code; nothing comes from the network, the environment, or package data. The same holds for 0.5.0, released on 2026-10-24.\n\nThis is documented in https://github.com/rcgiri-physics/physverify/blob/main/SECURITY.md, which advises running untrusted code only inside the project's sandbox container, and offers `physverify scan`, which only parses the source. Would you consider reclassifying the record as intended behaviour (or withdrawing it)? Happy to give any detail you need.\n\nRam Chandra Giri\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vulnetix/advisory-database/issues/7/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vulnetix/advisory-database/issues/7/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aidotmarket/ai-market-frontend/issues/238","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aidotmarket/ai-market-frontend","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aidotmarket/ai-market-frontend/issues/238/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aidotmarket/ai-market-frontend/issues/238/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aidotmarket/ai-market-frontend/issues/238/events","html_url":"https://github.com/aidotmarket/ai-market-frontend/pull/238","id":6022627367,"node_id":"PR_kwDOQ5oxVc8AAAABKjeQpw","number":238,"title":"Retire dashboard reads and setup continuations when the account visit ends","user":{"login":"maxrobbins","id":11612861,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNjEyODYx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11612861?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maxrobbins","html_url":"https://github.com/maxrobbins","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maxrobbins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maxrobbins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maxrobbins/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maxrobbins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maxrobbins/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maxrobbins/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maxrobbins/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maxrobbins/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maxrobbins/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-25T08:51:10Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T17:45:01Z","closed_at":"2026-10-25T17:45:01Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aidotmarket/ai-market-frontend/pulls/238","html_url":"https://github.com/aidotmarket/ai-market-frontend/pull/238","diff_url":"https://github.com/aidotmarket/ai-market-frontend/pull/238.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/aidotmarket/ai-market-frontend/pull/238.patch","merged_at":"2026-10-25T17:45:01Z"},"body":"A delayed seller overview response could replace another account’s figures, show an old failure, or finish its loading state after an account switch. Tie the dashboard visit to account identity and the existing authentication lifecycle, fencing capability, seller and purchase reads and later setup/onboarding/refresh/clipboard continuations. Retire private state on account change, authentication loss or departure; preserve ordinary token refresh and already admitted requests.\n\nFinal source e30cd6047272ed042d0f9d070ed951dcad575a2c integrates released status-label repair R570 through normal merge969a7097, preserving the reviewed dashboard ownership logic exactly. The only later fixture correction supplies inert subscribe() for the existing constant-state auth mock; all64 status assertions and the refusal guards remain unchanged. Existing dashboard test source remains byte-identical to reviewed92d72ca9. No Gateway source or behavior was changed.\n\nIndependent Astra: full1213da5b approved production9e5e590 (production/focused harness unchanged in final original92d); scoped integration8637a82a APPROVED969/e30 with no blocking findings and independently ran38 fake-port cases. Full final CC9e305f85 APPROVE_WITH_NITS, 0HIGH/0MEDIUM, Fable5.1HIGH aimarket; natural completion2026-10-25T17:42:08Z. Its3 advisory LOWs cover test-strength/static-only evidence, with no blocking production gap. All required review evidence is qualified; normal release verification remains.\n\nOriginal final automatic CI40212522325/job121226631577 passed4236tests/249files, including64 status,38 dashboard and101 Gateway cases; lint/typecheck passed. Its actual virtual merge64b5f67c, parents295fa+e30, has exactly candidate treec969ffbb. No manual rerun. Earlier969 originalCI failure history retained:17 status mock failures plus one Gateway focus case, subsequently101 GatewayPASS without an Athena Gateway source repair. Prior baseline and original source CI4171/248/38 retained separately.\n\nRoot integration verification proves all4 released delta paths equal the candidate and all other paths equal currentmaina67677b3 (R573 release); expected current uniontreed0c94225. The fetched GitHub PR preview64b5 still uses prior295fa base and is not proof of this newer union or its CI. No rebase or duplicate PR is needed; verify actual merge tree and original mainCI during normal release.\n\nChecks are qualified source/strict-VM fake ports and original hostedCI. Local whole Vitest, actual authenticated dashboard/backend/provider/customer/native/DB operations remain unverified and held. Capability/MFA policies, historical buyer/seller contracts and all security holds remain intact; full inherited16repo audit is incomplete.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aidotmarket/ai-market-frontend/issues/238/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aidotmarket/ai-market-frontend/issues/238/timeline","performed_via_github_app":{"id":1144995,"client_id":"Iv23liVemv8A9if9v0F2","slug":"chatgpt-codex-connector","node_id":"A_kwHOAOQ6Gs4AEXij","owner":{"login":"openai","id":14957082,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjE0OTU3MDgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14957082?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai","html_url":"https://github.com/openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/received_events","typ